<g fill="#FBF3E3"><circle cx="24" cy="100" r="2.2"/><circle cx="176" cy="100" r="2.2"/></g></svg><h1>Colombia <em>Classics</em></h1><div class="sub">THE BEST ROOFTOPS AND PLACES TO EAT</div><div class="ed">Cartagena Edition</div></div>
<div class="ph"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Colourful rooftop terrace in Cartagena"></div><div class="foot">OCTOBER 2026</div></section><section class="pg"><div class="eyebrow">MEET THE WRITER</div><h2 style="font-size:28pt;margin-top:3mm">Hello, I'm Kay</h2>
<div class="feature" style="grid-template-columns:84mm 1fr"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Kay on the beach in San Andrés" style="width:84mm;height:126mm;border-radius:42mm 42mm 3mm 3mm;object-position:center 65%">
<div><p class="lede" style="font-size:13pt">Picture me under the palms on San Andrés, sand between my toes and the sea every shade of turquoise. That's where this brochure began.</p>
<p style="margin-top:4mm">I'm a 54 year old luxury traveller and a former backpacker, so I know the joy of a five star rooftop and the joy of a hammock and a cold beer. I'm a travel and people development writer, and I travel as a single female traveller.</p>
<p style="margin-top:3mm">From hidden courtyards in Getsemaní to rooftops above the old walls, I seek out the places I'd recommend to a friend, and I share them as honestly as I can.</p>
<p style="margin-top:3mm">I created Colombia Classics to make it easy for other women to feel safe, confident and free to explore this beautiful country on their own terms.</p></div></div>
<div class="hero" style="margin-top:7mm"><div><h3>Every month, a new edition</h3><p>This brochure is free. Each month I share short stories and hidden gems for you to explore, and each of my brochures includes secret restaurants and hotels all over Colombia.</p></div>
<div><h3>£4.99 an edition</h3><p>Each new edition is £4.99, and every copy helps fund my next trip, so there's always a new place to share with you. Thank you for travelling with me.</p></div></div>
<p class="lede" style="text-align:center;margin-top:9mm;font-size:15pt;color:#0F4C45">Travel feeds the soul, and meeting people is beautiful. Enjoy.</p>
<p style="text-align:center;font-family:Cinzel,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:.2em;color:#B8913A;font-size:9pt;margin-top:2mm">KAY</p><div class="pgfoot"><span>COLOMBIA CLASSICS</span><span>02</span></div></section><section class="pg"><div class="eyebrow">WELCOME</div><h2 style="font-size:28pt;margin-top:3mm">Above the old walls</h2><div class="rule"></div>
<p class="lede">It's half past five in Cartagena. The heat is finally easing, the bells of the old town are ringing, and somewhere above the colourful balconies a cocktail is being poured as the sun slides into the bay. The best way to see this city is from its rooftops.</p>
<p style="margin-top:6mm">Colombia Classics brings together ten of Cartagena's finest rooftop terraces and the places worth staying for dinner. Some are hidden on the third floor of a colonial house in the old town, one sits on the 51st floor above Bocagrande, and others come with a pool, a DJ and a sun lounger waiting for you.</p>
<p style="margin-top:4mm">Every venue is marked <b style="color:#2F7F86;font-weight:500">Budget</b>, <b style="color:#B8913A;font-weight:500">Mid price</b> or <b style="color:#C8456E;font-weight:500">A real treat</b>, with the type of crowd you'll find, so you can choose the right rooftop for the evening you want. If you're travelling alone, our safety page has been written with you in mind.</p>
<div class="tips" style="margin-top:9mm">
<div class="tip"><h4>WHEN TO GO</h4><p>Arrive by 5pm for sunset. December to March is the driest and busiest season, so book ahead.</p></div>
<div class="tip"><h4>WHAT TO WEAR</h4><p>Casual chic works almost everywhere. Smart casual for hotel rooftops and dinner.</p></div>
<div class="tip"><h4>PRICES</h4><p>Prices are in Colombian pesos. Most rooftop cocktails cost between COP 40,000 and 75,000.</p></div>
