<div class="hero"><div><h3>Meeting others is easy at Selina</h3><p>With two rooftop pools, a house DJ and a social calendar, Selina is full of travellers, digital nomads and people who came to meet others. Pull up a lounger, order a cocktail and conversation tends to start on its own.</p></div>
<div><h3>And in Bocagrande</h3><p>Bocagrande's beachfront, hotels and high rise bars, including 51 Sky Bar, draw a sociable mix of visitors and locals. It's an easy, relaxed place to get chatting, whether you're on your own or with friends.</p></div></div>
<div class="crowd"><div><b>Mirador Culture Bar</b>Lively groups of friends and travellers, busy on music nights.</div><div><b>Apogeo Restaurante &amp; Rooftop</b>Couples and dinner groups, intimate and relaxed.</div><div><b>Casa Pura Rooftop</b>A stylish sunset crowd of couples and friends.</div><div><b>51 Sky Bar</b>Hotel guests, visitors and locals celebrating. Bocagrande is an easy place to get chatting.</div><div><b>Townhouse Rooftop</b>Social and sunny, with brunch groups by day and a party crowd at night.</div><div><b>Buena Vida Rooftop</b>Date nights and small groups of friends.</div><div><b>Alyzia Rooftop &amp; Dining</b>Couples, celebrations and hotel guests.</div><div><b>Alquímico</b>Cocktail lovers, locals and travellers, busy and buzzing.</div><div><b>Urania Rooftop</b>Relaxed and elegant, mostly couples and hotel guests.</div></div><div class="pgfoot"><span>COLOMBIA CLASSICS</span><span>11</span></div></section><section class="pg"><div class="eyebrow">TRAVELLING SOLO</div><h2 style="font-size:26pt;margin-top:3mm">Safety tips for women travelling alone</h2>
<p class="lede" style="font-size:11.5pt;margin-top:4mm">Cartagena is a joy to explore on your own, and thousands of women do it every year. A little local knowledge means you can relax, meet people and enjoy every sunset with confidence.</p>
<div class="safe">
<div><h4>Watch your drink</h4><p>Order your own drinks, watch them being made, and never leave a glass unattended. Politely decline drinks from strangers.</p></div>
<div><h4>Travel by registered taxi or app</h4><p>Ask your hotel or venue to call a taxi, or use a ride app, especially after dark. Share your trip with a friend.</p></div>
<div><h4>Stay where it's lively</h4><p>The walled city, Getsemaní and Bocagrande are busy into the evening. Avoid quiet streets and beaches alone at night.</p></div>
<div><h4>"No dar papaya"</h4><p>A local saying meaning don't make yourself an easy target. Keep your phone and jewellery out of sight in crowded streets.</p></div>
<div><h4>Be careful with dating apps</h4><p>Meet new people in busy public places, tell someone where you're going, and arrange your own transport.</p></div>
<div><h4>Carry the essentials</h4><p>Keep a photo of your passport, a little cash in a separate pocket, and use ATMs inside banks or shopping centres.</p></div>
<div><h4>Stay connected</h4><p>Share your location with someone you trust, and keep your phone charged before a night out.</p></div>
<div><h4>Know the numbers</h4><p>The emergency number in Colombia is 123. Save your hotel's number and your embassy's details in your phone.</p></div></div>
<div class="tips" style="margin-top:5mm"><div class="tip"><h4>MEET PEOPLE SAFELY</h4><p>Social hotels like Selina and group tours are great ways to meet other travellers in a relaxed setting.</p></div>
<div class="tip"><h4>TRUST YOUR INSTINCTS</h4><p>If somewhere doesn't feel right, leave. Venue staff and hotel teams are there to help.</p></div></div><div class="pgfoot"><span>COLOMBIA CLASSICS</span><span>12</span></div></section><section class="pg"><div class="eyebrow">STAY FOR DINNER</div><h2 style="font-size:26pt;margin-top:3mm">Places to eat, Colombia Classics style</h2>
<p class="lede" style="margin-top:4mm">The sun has gone, the string lights are on, and nobody wants to leave. Several of our rooftops are just as good for dinner as they are for drinks.</p>
<div class="also" style="grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;margin-top:6mm">
<div><h4>For a celebration</h4><p>Alyzia or Apogeo, for a table with a view and a menu to linger over.</p></div>
<div><h4>For seafood</h4><p>Buena Vida, three floors of Caribbean flavour in the heart of the old town.</p></div>
<div><h4>For Colombian flavours</h4><p>Mar y Zielo, inspired by journeys across the country.</p></div>
<div><h4>For a long, lazy brunch</h4><p>Townhouse or Urania, with the morning sun and the rooftops below.</p></div></div>
<div class="tips" style="margin-top:6mm"><div class="tip"><h4>GOOD TO KNOW</h4><p>Hotel pools are usually for guests only, though some offer day passes.</p></div>
<div class="tip"><h4>DRINK WATER</h4><p>Cartagena is hot and humid all year, so alternate cocktails with water.</p></div></div>
